-- title:
--   Preserving a memory prefix preserves the complete selected-color payload
-- statement:
--   Let $x:\operatorname{Fin}(n)\to\mathbb Z$, let $c$ be a color parameter for $\operatorname{inputBits}(n)+1$ bits, and let $A,B,C$ be strictly increasing integer lists. Suppose memory $\mu$ satisfies the selected-color pipeline's stored-data contract at base $f$: normalized color classes, primes, cover keys, wanted data, retained sources, lifts, and the final eight-cell header are all present. Let $F$ be the payload's final-header address. If $F+8\le t$ and memories $\mu,\nu$ agree below $t$, then
--   $$
--   \operatorname{Stored}(\mu,f,n,c,x,A,B,C)
--   \Longrightarrow\operatorname{Stored}(\nu,f,n,c,x,A,B,C).
--   $$
--   This lets later stages extend memory while retaining the complete earlier pipeline result and its associated count bounds.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/EncodedColorPipelineRetention.lean#L35-L71

